Session 30 summary — two criteria fixed, the remaining blocker isolated with a decisive instrument built and ready:

**Fixed and verified:**
1. **`online_resize` PASSES.** The fail was arithmetic, not a resize bug: sess21's 64MB/slice log minimum (4×64MB) + the 96MB envelope = 352MB fixed overhead, which a 90%-of-total-device gate can't absorb on a 2GB loop device. Measured proof: resize recovered exactly 1024MB = 100% of the added space. Gate now asserts `delta >= 90% of added space` with full justification in the script header.
2. **`chk_clean` PASSES (2/2 + in-gate).** RULE-4-proven root in both directions: an idle node unmounting last folds its stale mount-time percpu counters into the on-disk SB (ifree 61 over the writer's 28). Fix: `xfs_log_quiesce` now recomputes summary counters from on-disk AGF/AGI via `xfs_initialize_perag_data`, gated on a new sticky `m_mxfs_dlm_was_active` flag — `put_super` NULLs `m_mxfs_dlm` before `xfs_unmountfs`, which also silently broke `xfs_log_check_lsn`'s multi-node bypass (-EFSCORRUPTED at quiesce); both now use the sticky flag.
3. **`verify_ship.sh` got a node warm-up prologue** — the first criterion after a VM reboot was eating the whole cold-prep cost inside its 60s watchdog and dying with no RESULT line.

**Remaining blocker — `cache_coherency` (gate criteria 1–10 otherwise PASS):** one node's entire batch of same-dir modifications (creates or renames, rotating) durably reverts. Proven trigger: requires inode reuse from a preceding `test_cross_visibility` run (standalone rename passes 8/8). Built `scripts/diag_rename_loss.sh` (passive — active `ls` watchers suppress the bug) which catches it within ~2 attempts with full dmesg. Always-on probes were rate-limited into gaps, so the new build `987735E8AB5A4F7E184945E` adds a standalone `mxfs.dirwr=1` knob enabling only the `P-DIRWR` write trace (now with a content crc hashed past the LSN header) plus a new `P-DIRRD` read-completion sibling — merging those per-daddr across nodes will name the node that RMW'd the dir block from a stale base. Next session: deploy that build to test1-4, run the diag with `dirwr=1`, and follow the crc lineage to the producer. All details are in memory `sess30-run14d-resize-chkclean-fixed-rename-loss-hunt`.

